            <ArticleTitle>Nifedipine relieves exercise-exacerbated myalgias.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>647-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three women with exercise-exacerbated myalgias refractory to usual medications are described who responded favorably when the calcium channel blocker, nifedipine, was administered. The side effects were dose-related and prevented complete resolution of the symptoms. Three potential mechanisms of action are suggested for these effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
